{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791627393,"nonce":"E2psUNBJYiuwyP3vAx5zYbhbGPM=","message":"Live motion trace from cn_demo (dev build) showed the loop asking for frames at 16ms, but the frame that opens an overlay or switches tabs costing 140-170ms: ~100ms in phase 1, ~45ms in the paint. CSS animations, transitions, FLIP and motions advanced by the whole gap, so a 150ms fade showed one partial frame and was done on the next; tab transitions stepped 30-60ms.\n\ncn_profile (cn_demo's real UI built offscreen with WindowedContext::headless, dev build) located the phase-1 cost: after an update that needs layout, the windowed loop runs apply_stylesheet_layout_overrides over the whole tree, which wrote every class-driven style back, unchanged ones included; each write marked the node and its ancestors dirty, so compute_layout then took ~60ms instead of ~4ms.\n\nLanded: 494ec172 set_style leaves an unchanged style alone (tab switch layout 60ms -\u003e 4.5ms in cn_profile); 4cc5a964 a step is capped at 50ms (MAX_ANIMATION_STEP_MS), as ashui's MAX_STEP, so a slow frame pauses an animation instead of skipping it; b70124ca scheduler tick_by for deterministic offscreen runs; fe607d56 BLINC_MOTION_TRACE per-frame trace; c6e9019f WindowedContext::headless + cn_profile.\n\nStill to confirm in the live app with a new trace: the overlay-open frame cost, and the 40-65ms full paints (offscreen GPU paint of the same tree is ~10ms at 900x900, 1x).","files":null}]}